    "query": "online ms nursing programs in maryland",
    "response": "**Universities Offering Online MSN Programs in Maryland**\n\n* **Johns Hopkins University:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN)\n    * Specializations: Adult-Gerontology Nurse Practitioner, Family Nurse Practitioner, Pediatric Nurse Practitioner\n\n* **University of Maryland, Baltimore:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN)\n    * Specializations: Adult-Gerontology Primary Care Nurse Practitioner, Family Nurse Practitioner, Pediatric Nurse Practitioner, Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner\n\n* **University of Maryland, Eastern Shore:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) with Family Nurse Practitioner Concentration\n\n* **Coppin State University:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) with Family Nurse Practitioner or Nurse Educator Concentration\n\n* **Loyola University Maryland:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN)\n    * Specializations: Adult-Gerontology Nurse Practitioner, Family Nurse Practitioner, Nurse Educator\n\n* **George Mason University:**\n    * Master of Science in Nursing (MSN)\n    * Specializations: Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, Family Nurse Practitioner, Pediatric Nurse Practitioner\n\n**Additional Information**\n\n* The MSN is typically a 36-60 credit program that can be completed in 1-3 years of full-time study.\n* Many programs offer flexible scheduling, including online and hybrid options.\n* Most universities require a bachelor's degree in nursing or a related field for admission.\n* The cost of an online MSN program varies depending on the university and program length.\n* Graduates of online MSN programs are eligible for national certification from organizations such as the American Nurses Credentialing Center (ANCC) and the American Academy of Nurse Practitioners (AANP).",
